1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,600
Right now,

2
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,033
you're probably hearing a lot about Dominion Energy's

3
00:00:03,033 --> 00:00:04,933
$67 billion takeover

4
00:00:04,933 --> 00:00:06,300
by NextEra Energy.

5
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:08,600
But while the merger debate dominates the headlines,

6
00:00:08,633 --> 00:00:11,133
customers of Virginia's second-largest utility monopoly

7
00:00:11,133 --> 00:00:14,100
are facing yet another increase in their energy bills.

8
00:00:14,166 --> 00:00:15,066
That's right.

9
00:00:15,066 --> 00:00:17,500
If Appalachian Power Company is your electric provider,

10
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:19,833
your bills could be going up again.

11
00:00:20,233 --> 00:00:22,800
Is justifying its request by pointing to factors

12
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:25,433
including inflation, storm recovery expenses

13
00:00:25,433 --> 00:00:27,200
and higher capital costs. But

14
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:28,833
what nobody is talking about

15
00:00:28,833 --> 00:00:30,400
is the elephant in the room:

16
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:33,866
their profit, which is fixed and guaranteed by the state.

17
00:00:33,866 --> 00:00:35,833
It's referred to as return on equity,

18
00:00:35,833 --> 00:00:38,000
or ROE. And in Virginia,

19
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,900
overinflated ROE is one of the biggest cost drivers

20
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:42,300
of rising energy bills.

21
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:44,833
It's an issue that lawmakers representing Southwest Virginia

22
00:00:44,833 --> 00:00:47,500
tried to fix during the legislative session last year,

23
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:49,600
but challenging utilities' profit

24
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:52,066
means going up against some of the most powerful

25
00:00:52,066 --> 00:00:54,200
corporate lobbying capacity in the state.

26
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:56,733
So ultimately, the bill died.

27
00:00:56,900 --> 00:01:02,466
Now, APCo is currently authorized to earn a 9.75% ROE,

28
00:01:02,466 --> 00:01:04,566
which is already incredibly high,

29
00:01:04,566 --> 00:01:08,033
but it's asking to increase that to 10.5%.

30
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:10,066
The good news is, if you're an APCo customer,

31
00:01:10,066 --> 00:01:12,400
it's not too late to weigh in on what happens next,

32
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:15,066
and you can do it from the comfort of your own home.

33
00:01:15,133 --> 00:01:17,966
The SCC will hear public testimony by phone

34
00:01:17,966 --> 00:01:20,200
at 10 a.m. on October 19th.

35
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:24,033
To sign up, visit scc.virginia.gov.

36
00:01:24,033 --> 00:01:27,666
Under the Cases tab, click on Participating in SCC Cases,

37
00:01:27,666 --> 00:01:31,000
then scroll down until you see Testifying by Telephone.

38
00:01:31,033 --> 00:01:32,933
Click on the Public Witness Appearance Form

39
00:01:32,933 --> 00:01:34,900
and include the SCC case number,

40
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:40,700
PUR-2026-00044, along with your contact information.

41
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:41,566
That's it.

42
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:44,600
The SCC will call you on the morning of October 19th

43
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:45,933
to hear your testimony.

44
00:01:46,033 --> 00:01:48,166
The deadline to register is October 15th,

45
00:01:48,166 --> 00:01:50,100
so mark your calendars, sign up

46
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:51,533
and make your voice heard.
